      "content": "I would recommend taking your 14-month-old to the emergency room, as diarrhea can be a sign of an underlying infection or dehydration, especially in young children. Giving him diluted apple juice may not be enough to fully rehydrate him, and he may still be at risk for complications like electrolyte imbalances or shock. Dehydration can cause a range of symptoms, including lethargy, difficulty waking up, and not urinating. Please seek medical attention to ensure his safety and proper treatment.",
